  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will build\nnorthward over the Silver State this afternoon through Wednesday.\nThis ridge of high pressure will progress eastward Wednesday night\nand Thursday. High temperatures across Northern and Central Nevada each\nafternoon today through Thursday will be around ten degrees above\nnormal for this time of year. An Eastern Pacific storm system\nwill approach the west coast of the United States Friday. As a\nresult, the surface pressure gradient will increase. Sustained\nsouth winds 20 to 30 mph, with gusts near 50 mph are possible in\nCentral Nevada Friday into early Saturday morning. A Wind Advisory\nmay be required. \n\nA trough of low pressure will pass eastward across Northern and\nCentral Nevada Friday evening through Saturday morning, resulting\nin a chance of valley rain and mountain snow. Snow levels will\nstart at around 8,500 feet Friday evening, before dropping to\nabout 7,000 feet by Saturday morning. There will be a brief break\nin precipitation the remainder of the upcoming weekend, prior to\nthe next storm system Monday and Monday night. Snow levels will\nstart at around 7,000 feet Monday, before dropping to about 5,500\nfeet Monday night. Here are probabilities of one tenth of an inch\nof rain or more for select locations in Northern and Central\nNevada Monday and Monday night:\n\nAustin - 90%\nElko - 85%\nSpring Creek - 85%\nEly - 85%\nTonopah - 85%\nWinnemucca - 75%\nCarlin - 75%\nWells - 75%\nEureka - 75%\nJackpot - 75%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence in\nunseasonably warm weather today through Thursday. Moderate\nforecast confidence regarding strong wind gusts in Central Nevada\nFriday into early Saturday morning. Moderate forecast confidence\nin precipitation Friday evening through Saturday morning. Low\nforecast confidence regarding periods of precipitation Monday and\nMonday night.",
